# Module input — Validate & form feedback

Check **shape and type** of user input here. After validation passes, escape for SQL with `module-sql.mdc`. Protect HTTP entrypoints with `module-security.mdc`.

Per [PrestaShop good practices](https://devdocs.prestashop-project.org/9/modules/creation/good-practices/): validate customer/merchant input; show confirmation or error on configuration forms.

## Read request data safely

```php
$idProduct = (int) Tools::getValue('id_product');
$email     = Tools::getValue('email');
$label     = Tools::getValue('label');
```

Never trust raw `$_GET` / `$_POST`. Always validate before `Configuration::updateValue`, `Db` writes, or outbound API calls.

## PrestaShop `Validate` (common checks)

| Input | Check |
|---|---|
| Integer ID | `Validate::isUnsignedId($id)` or cast `(int)` when zero is invalid |
| Price / decimal | `Validate::isPrice($value)` |
| Email | `Validate::isEmail($email)` |
| URL | `Validate::isUrl($url)` |
| Generic name / reference | `Validate::isGenericName($str)` or module-specific rule |
| HTML fields | `Validate::isCleanHtml($html, true)` when rich text is allowed |
| Module name token | `Validate::isModuleName($name)` |

On failure: collect an error string and **do not** save or call external APIs.

```php
if (!Validate::isUnsignedId($idProduct)) {
    $this->errors[] = $this->l('Invalid product ID.');
    return;
}
```

## Back-office forms

Every settings / configuration submit must:

1. **Validate** all fields (reject early with specific messages).
2. **Save** only when `$this->errors` (or the module's error array) is empty.
3. **Confirm** success — e.g. `$this->confirmations[] = $this->l('Settings updated.');` or the module's existing flash pattern.
4. **Re-display** invalid values only after validation failed; never echo unescaped user input in templates.

User-visible strings go through `$this->l()` and `module-translations.mdc` (EN/FR/ES parity).

## Order of operations

```
Request → Validate (this rule) → token/session check (module-security) → SQL escape (module-sql) → Db / Configuration / API
```

Do not skip validation because `pSQL()` will be applied later — escaping is not validation.

## Never

- Save `Tools::getValue(...)` to DB or config without a `Validate` check or explicit whitelist.
- Silent failure on invalid form posts (no error message).
- Concatenate inside `$this->l()` — translate literals first (`module-translations.mdc`).
